<tr id="S1.T1.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T1.4.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">2D AD</th>
<td id="S1.T1.3.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S1.T1.3.3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="51\times 51" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>51</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>51</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">51\times 51</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T1.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">61</td>
<td id="S1.T1.4.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S1.T1.4.4.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-5,5]^{2}\times[0,6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-5,5]^{2}\times[0,6]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T1.4.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">520</td>
<td id="S1.T1.4.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">12</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table S1: </span>Benchmark grids and observation counts. S20 reports the number of
fixed spatial sensors observed at every time frame; T20 reports the number
of retained frames observed on the complete spatial grid.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The primary fixed-library comparison uses clean observations under two
complementary 20% sampling protocols. In S20, each seed samples spatial
locations uniformly without replacement and observes the same sensor set at
every time frame. In T20, the initial frame is retained and the remaining
frames are sampled uniformly without replacement to form an irregular
temporal subset observed on the complete spatial grid. We evaluate the five
test seeds <math id="S1.SS1.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1301,1709,2203,2917,3571\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1301</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1709</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2203</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2917</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3571</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1301,1709,2203,2917,3571\}</annotation></semantics></math> for every benchmark and protocol.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each benchmark, protocol, and seed, a shared observation record stores the
sampled coordinates and values, the spatial masks, and the retained time
indices. Every method receives the same record. Methods that fit continuous
surrogates may evaluate those surrogates at additional coordinates for
automatic differentiation or weak integration, but only the sampled values
enter model fitting. Dense reference values are used exclusively to compute
evaluation metrics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The shared physical candidate libraries are</p>
<table id="S8.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{KdV/KS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>KdV</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>KS</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{KdV/KS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[1,u,u^{2},u^{3},uu_{x},u_{xx},u_{xxx},u_{xxxx}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[1,u,u^{2},u^{3},uu_{x},u_{xx},u_{xxx},u_{xxxx}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S1)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{2D\,AD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>AD</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Theta_{\mathrm{2D\,AD}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[1,u,u^{2},u_{x},u_{y},u_{xx},u_{yy}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[1,u,u^{2},u_{x},u_{y},u_{xx},u_{yy}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S2)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These physical libraries are fixed before evaluation and shared by all
methods. Algebraically equivalent conservative terms are mapped to the
displayed convention before support and coefficient scoring; for example,
<math id="S1.SS1.p4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{x}(u^{2})=2uu_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{x}(u^{2})=2uu_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Metrics and Aggregation</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We evaluate structural recovery separately from coefficient and field
accuracy. Exact recovery requires equality between the selected support
<math id="S1.SS2.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the true support <math id="S1.SS2.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define support
<math id="S1.SS2.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as the harmonic mean of precision and recall over candidate terms. The
relative coefficient and field errors are</p>
<table id="S1.E3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S1.E3X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E3X.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E3X.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\lVert\hat{\xi}-\xi^{\star}\rVert_{2}}{\lVert\xi^{\star}\rVert_{2}+10^{-12}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\lVert\hat{\xi}-\xi^{\star}\rVert_{2}}{\lVert\xi^{\star}\rVert_{2}+10^{-12}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(S3)</span></td>
</tr>
<tr id="S1.E3Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E3Xa.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E_{u}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E3Xa.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\lVert\hat{u}-u^{\star}\rVert_{2}}{\lVert u^{\star}\rVert_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\lVert\hat{u}-u^{\star}\rVert_{2}}{\lVert u^{\star}\rVert_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Before computing <math id="S1.SS2.p1.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\xi}</annotation></semantics></math>, each selected equation is expressed in the shared
physical basis defined in Sec. A.1, with zero coefficients assigned to absent
terms. Field error is evaluated on the complete reference grid.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The fixed library results report exact recoveries out of five runs and medians
over the same five runs. Curves in the observation density study report
medians and interquartile ranges. In the symbolic experiment, continuous
parameters are summarized as mean <math id="S1.SS2.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math> sample standard deviation over runs
that recover the target power-law structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Structured Field Adapter and Training</h3>

<div id="S1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.11" class="ltx_p">The structured field adapter reconstructs the continuous field as</p>
<table id="S1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{u}_{\eta,C}(x,t)=b_{\eta}(x)+\Phi_{\eta}(x)^{\top}C\bar{\beta}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{u}_{\eta,C}(x,t)=b_{\eta}(x)+\Phi_{\eta}(x)^{\top}C\bar{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S4)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">using only the sampled observations. A spatial MLP jointly produces the
background <math id="S1.SS3.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\eta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\eta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS3.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> spatial features <math id="S1.SS3.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\eta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\eta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Its input is
the random Fourier encoding
<math id="S1.SS3.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(\tilde{x})=[\sin(B\tilde{x}),\cos(B\tilde{x})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(\tilde{x})=[\sin(B\tilde{x}),\cos(B\tilde{x})]</annotation></semantics></math>, where the 64 rows of <math id="S1.SS3.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>
are sampled once per run from a standard Gaussian distribution and then held
fixed. The hidden layers use Swish activations. Here <math id="S1.SS3.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{x}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{x}=x</annotation></semantics></math> for KdV and
KS, while each coordinate of 2D AD is divided by 5 before Fourier encoding.
The temporal vector <math id="S1.SS3.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a clamped uniform cubic B-spline basis
centered by subtracting its empirical mean over the observed time locations,
with <math id="S1.SS3.p1.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> internal knots and <math id="S1.SS3.p1.9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=K+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=K+4</annotation></semantics></math> basis functions. The matrix
<math id="S1.SS3.p1.10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{R\times M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{R\times M}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the trainable spline coefficients. S20
and T20 use the same adapter configuration; they differ only in the
coordinates and values supplied to the reconstruction loss.
Table <a href="#S1.T2" title="Table S2 ‣ A.3 Structured Field Adapter and Training ‣ A Experimental Details ‣ Freeze, Then Select: Structured Field Adapters and Stability-Validated Weak Selection for PDE Discovery from Sparse Observations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S2</span></a> lists the benchmark-specific architecture
sizes and maximum training epochs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S1.T2.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S1.T2.4.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T2.4.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">PDE</th>
<th id="S1.T2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Rank <math id="S1.T2.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>
</th>
<th id="S1.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Hidden width <math id="S1.T2.2.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> layers</th>
<th id="S1.T2.3.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Internal knots <math id="S1.T2.3.3.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>
</th>
<th id="S1.T2.4.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Basis size <math id="S1.T2.4.4.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>
</th>
<th id="S1.T2.4.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Trainable parameters</th>
<th id="S1.T2.4.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">Maximum epochs</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S1.T2.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">KdV</td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">12</td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;"><math id="S1.T2.5.5.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\!\times\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\!\times\!3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">32</td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">36</td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">17,853</td>
<td id="S1.T2.5.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">5,000</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S1.T2.6.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">KS</td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">24</td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;"><math id="S1.T2.6.6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\!\times\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\!\times\!3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">64</td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">68</td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">19,833</td>
<td id="S1.T2.6.6.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">5,500</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S1.T2.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">2D AD</td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">16</td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;"><math id="S1.T2.7.7.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="72\!\times\!3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>72</mn><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">72\!\times\!3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">6</td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">10</td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">21,201</td>
<td id="S1.T2.7.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.2pt;padding-right:4.2pt;">5,500</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table S2: </span>Structured adapter settings. All models use Swish activations and
the random Fourier encoding described above. Trainable parameter counts
include the spatial MLP and <math id="S1.T2.9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">The adapter is trained from observations without a PDE residual:</p>
<table id="S1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\eta,C}\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obs}}+\lambda_{\Phi}\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}+\lambda_{t}\mathcal{R}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\eta,C}\;\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obs}}+\lambda_{\Phi}\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}+\lambda_{t}\mathcal{R}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S5)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S8.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{obs}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{obs}}}\sum_{i}\left|\widehat{u}_{\eta,C}(x_{i},t_{i})-y_{i}\right|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>obs</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{obs}}}\sum_{i}\left|\widehat{u}_{\eta,C}(x_{i},t_{i})-y_{i}\right|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S6)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|\frac{1}{N_{g}}\Phi_{\eta}(X_{g})^{\top}\Phi_{\eta}(X_{g})-I\right\|_{F}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|\frac{1}{N_{g}}\Phi_{\eta}(X_{g})^{\top}\Phi_{\eta}(X_{g})-I\right\|_{F}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S7)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S1.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{R}\int_{0}^{T}|c_{r}^{\prime\prime}(t)|^{2}\,dt," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{r=1}^{R}\int_{0}^{T}|c_{r}^{\prime\prime}(t)|^{2}\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S8)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S1.SS3.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="S1.SS3.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> points sampled uniformly from the spatial domain
and <math id="S1.SS3.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{r}(t)=C_{r:}\bar{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi></mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{r}(t)=C_{r:}\bar{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is the coefficient of spatial feature <math id="S1.SS3.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Gram penalty <math id="S1.SS3.p2.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\Phi}</annotation></semantics></math> uses 512 uniformly sampled spatial points
per update, and the temporal curvature integral is approximated on a uniform
200-point time grid.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS3.p3.8" class="ltx_p">Training uses AdamW with an initial learning rate of <math id="S1.SS3.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, a cosine
decay schedule over the maximum epoch budget, weight decay <math id="S1.SS3.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
global gradient-norm clipping at 1.0. During the first 400 epochs, <math id="S1.SS3.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is
fixed at zero to fit the background component. Afterward, <math id="S1.SS3.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS3.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are
optimized jointly. For KdV and KS, both regularization weights are zero for
the first 800 epochs and increase linearly over the next 1,600 epochs; for 2D
AD, the corresponding periods are 600 and 1,200 epochs. Their target weights
are <math id="S1.SS3.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\Phi}=3\times 10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\Phi}=3\times 10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS3.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}=5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}=5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. The weighted
feature and temporal penalties are capped at 0.15 and 0.25 times the current
observation loss, respectively. Each update samples at most 32 observed time
frames and uses all spatial observations available at those frames. The MSE
over all observations selects the lowest-loss reconstruction checkpoint among
those tracked after the 400-epoch background phase. Early stopping begins at
the same point and uses a patience of 800 epochs and a minimum decrease of
<math id="S1.SS3.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>. The selected checkpoint is frozen before any weak system is
constructed; equation selection does not feed back into adapter training.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">B </span>Stability-Validated Weak Selection</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Weak System Construction and Continuity</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.18" class="ltx_p">Consider a candidate equation written as</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}=\sum_{j}\xi_{j}\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}q_{j}(u)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}=\sum_{j}\xi_{j}\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}q_{j}(u),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S9)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}\in\mathbb{N}_{0}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}=\partial_{x}^{\alpha_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0.1389em">∂</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}=\partial_{x}^{\alpha_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar
function of the state. The case <math id="S2.SS1.p1.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> covers algebraic terms, and the
formal adjoint is
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}=(-1)^{|\alpha_{j}|}\partial_{x}^{\alpha_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}=(-1)^{|\alpha_{j}|}\partial_{x}^{\alpha_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a compactly supported test function <math id="S2.SS1.p1.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>,
integration by parts transfers the derivatives to <math id="S2.SS1.p1.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>.

The corresponding weak entries are</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10X.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{\ell}(\widehat{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{\ell}(\widehat{u})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10X.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\langle\widehat{u},\partial_{t}\psi_{\ell}\rangle_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\langle\widehat{u},\partial_{t}\psi_{\ell}\rangle_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(S10)</span></td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10Xa.2.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\ell j}(\widehat{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\ell j}(\widehat{u})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10Xa.3.2.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle q_{j}(\widehat{u}),\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}\psi_{\ell}\rangle_{\ell}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle q_{j}(\widehat{u}),\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}\psi_{\ell}\rangle_{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.13" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes integration over patch
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. These entries form the regression system
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\widehat{u})\approx A(\widehat{u})\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\widehat{u})\approx A(\widehat{u})\xi</annotation></semantics></math>. For a patch centered at <math id="S2.SS1.p1.11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>,
with spatial and temporal
half-widths <math id="S2.SS1.p1.12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\ell,a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\ell,a}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\ell,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\ell,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use</p>
<table id="S8.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{p}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{p}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-s^{2})^{p}\mathbf{1}\{|s|&lt;1\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-s^{2})^{p}\mathbf{1}\{|s|&lt;1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S11)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{\ell}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{\ell}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\rho_{p}\!\left(\frac{t-c_{\ell,t}}{h_{\ell,t}}\right)\prod_{a=1}^{d}\rho_{p}\!\left(\frac{x_{a}-c_{\ell,a}}{h_{\ell,a}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\rho_{p}\!\left(\frac{t-c_{\ell,t}}{h_{\ell,t}}\right)\prod_{a=1}^{d}\rho_{p}\!\left(\frac{x_{a}-c_{\ell,a}}{h_{\ell,a}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S12)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.17" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="S2.SS1.p1.14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and its derivatives through order <math id="S2.SS1.p1.15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-1</annotation></semantics></math> vanish at
<math id="S2.SS1.p1.16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math>, choosing <math id="S2.SS1.p1.17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> above the highest derivative order in each candidate
library eliminates the boundary terms introduced by integration by parts.
Spatial derivatives therefore act on the known test function rather than
pointwise on the reconstructed field. This construction uses values from the
frozen adapter while avoiding direct evaluation of its higher-order spatial
derivatives.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Patch centers form a regular grid inside the admissible domain. Each weak
system applies an independently sampled phase shift to this grid. The field,
observations, and candidate library remain unchanged; only the integration
patches differ. This produces multiple views of the same frozen reconstruction
and provides the variation used by SVWS to assess support stability. All
integrals are evaluated using midpoint tensor grids.
Table <a href="#S2.T3" title="Table S3 ‣ B.1 Weak System Construction and Continuity ‣ B Stability-Validated Weak Selection ‣ Freeze, Then Select: Structured Field Adapters and Stability-Validated Weak Selection for PDE Discovery from Sparse Observations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S3</span></a> lists the corresponding settings for each
benchmark.</p>
</div>
