<th id="S2.T3.3.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">3,000</th>
<td id="S2.T3.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.2.2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.3.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.3.3.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.3.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">8</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.T3.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T3.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">KS</th>
<th id="S2.T3.5.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">300</th>
<th id="S2.T3.5.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">3,100</th>
<td id="S2.T3.4.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.4.4.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.5.5.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.5.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">8</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.T3.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T3.7.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">2D AD</th>
<th id="S2.T3.7.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">320</th>
<th id="S2.T3.7.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">2,280</th>
<td id="S2.T3.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.6.6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1.6,1.6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1.6,1.6)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.7.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><math id="S2.T3.7.7.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.48" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.48</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.48</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S2.T3.7.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">4</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table S3: </span>Weak system settings for each benchmark. Nodes per patch give the
effective size of the midpoint tensor grid; all half-widths are in physical
coordinates.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.8" class="ltx_p">For the exact weak entries, suppose that <math id="S2.SS1.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,\widehat{u}\in L_{2}(P_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,\widehat{u}\in L_{2}(P_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>, the
required derivatives of <math id="S2.SS1.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="S2.SS1.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}(P_{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}(P_{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S2.SS1.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on an interval containing the essential ranges of <math id="S2.SS1.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S2.SS1.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{u}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S2.SS1.p3.8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="S8.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|b_{\ell}(\widehat{u})-b_{\ell}(u)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|b_{\ell}(\widehat{u})-b_{\ell}(u)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\widehat{u}-u\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}\|\partial_{t}\psi_{\ell}\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\widehat{u}-u\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}\|\partial_{t}\psi_{\ell}\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S13)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|A_{\ell j}(\widehat{u})-A_{\ell j}(u)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|A_{\ell j}(\widehat{u})-A_{\ell j}(u)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L_{j}\|\widehat{u}-u\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L_{j}\|\widehat{u}-u\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
</tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\times\|\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}\psi_{\ell}\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi></mi><mo lspace="1.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\times\|\mathcal{D}_{\alpha_{j}}^{*}\psi_{\ell}\|_{L_{2}(P_{\ell})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S14)</span></td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.9" class="ltx_p">These bounds follow from the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality and establish
entrywise continuity of the exact weak system in the local reconstruction
error under the stated range condition. The midpoint discretization satisfies
analogous bounds in the corresponding quadrature-weighted norm. Comparing
independently shifted systems then allows SVWS to favor supports that remain
stable across weak discretizations. Support recovery also depends on library
conditioning, trajectory excitation, and coefficient separation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Selection Algorithm and Configuration</h3>

<figure id="S2.SS2.35" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div>
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S2.SS2.35.36" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Algorithm S1: Stability-Validated Weak Selection on a frozen field</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_flex_break"></div>
<span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div>
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS2.35.37" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel">
<table id="S2.SS2.35.35" class="ltx_tabular ltx_figure_panel ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S2.SS2.7.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.7.7.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom:2.0pt;" colspan="2">
<span id="S2.SS2.7.7.7.7.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.7.7.7.7.7.7" class="ltx_p" style="width:433.6pt;"><span id="S2.SS2.7.7.7.7.7.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> frozen field <math id="S2.SS2.1.1.1.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{u}</annotation></semantics></math>; candidate library; base threshold <math id="S2.SS2.2.2.2.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>; multipliers <math id="S2.SS2.3.3.3.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>; system counts <math id="S2.SS2.4.4.4.4.4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{g},R_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{g},R_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>; independent phase seeds; stability threshold <math id="S2.SS2.5.5.5.5.5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>; ridge parameter <math id="S2.SS2.6.6.6.6.6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; numerical constant <math id="S2.SS2.7.7.7.7.7.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S2.SS2.10.10.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.10.10.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">1</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.10.10.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.10.10.10.3.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.10.10.10.3.3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Build independently phased weak systems <math id="S2.SS2.8.8.8.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(A_{\mathrm{gen}}^{r},b_{\mathrm{gen}}^{r})\}_{r=1}^{R_{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>gen</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>gen</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(A_{\mathrm{gen}}^{r},b_{\mathrm{gen}}^{r})\}_{r=1}^{R_{g}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.9.9.9.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{\mathrm{fit}},b_{\mathrm{fit}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{\mathrm{fit}},b_{\mathrm{fit}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.10.10.10.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(A_{\mathrm{val}}^{s},b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s})\}_{s=1}^{R_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>val</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>val</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(A_{\mathrm{val}}^{s},b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s})\}_{s=1}^{R_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the same frozen field.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.13.13.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.13.13.13.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">2</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.13.13.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.13.13.13.3.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.13.13.13.3.3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">For each <math id="S2.SS2.11.11.11.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,m)\in\{1,\ldots,R_{g}\}\times\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,m)\in\{1,\ldots,R_{g}\}\times\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, run STLSQ at threshold <math id="S2.SS2.12.12.12.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> on the column-normalized generation system and record support <math id="S2.SS2.13.13.13.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{r,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{r,m}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.18.18.18" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.18.18.18.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">3</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.18.18.18.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.18.18.18.5.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.18.18.18.5.5.5" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Deduplicate the supports to form <math id="S2.SS2.14.14.14.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="S2.SS2.15.15.15.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, record its generation count <math id="S2.SS2.16.16.16.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(\mathcal{S})=\sum_{r,m}\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{S}_{r,m}=\mathcal{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(\mathcal{S})=\sum_{r,m}\mathbf{1}\{\mathcal{S}_{r,m}=\mathcal{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute term frequencies <math id="S2.SS2.17.17.17.4.4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{j}=(R_{g}|\mathcal{M}|)^{-1}\sum_{r,m}\mathbf{1}\{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r,m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{j}=(R_{g}|\mathcal{M}|)^{-1}\sum_{r,m}\mathbf{1}\{j\in\mathcal{S}_{r,m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and stable terms <math id="S2.SS2.18.18.18.5.5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\tau}=\{j:\pi_{j}\geq\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\tau}=\{j:\pi_{j}\geq\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.20.20.20" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.20.20.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">4</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.20.20.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.20.20.20.2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.20.20.20.2.2.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Retain <math id="S2.SS2.19.19.19.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\tau}=\{\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}:\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{J}_{\tau}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\tau}=\{\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}:\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{J}_{\tau}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. If this set is empty, set <math id="S2.SS2.20.20.20.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\tau}=\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\tau}=\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.26.26.26" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.26.26.26.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">5</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.26.26.26.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.26.26.26.6.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.26.26.26.6.6.6" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Let <math id="S2.SS2.21.21.21.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{fit}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{fit}}</annotation></semantics></math> contain the fit-system column norms and set <math id="S2.SS2.22.22.22.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{A}_{\mathrm{fit}}=A_{\mathrm{fit}}D_{\mathrm{fit}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>fit</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{A}_{\mathrm{fit}}=A_{\mathrm{fit}}D_{\mathrm{fit}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S2.SS2.23.23.23.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}_{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}_{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, fit <math id="S2.SS2.24.24.24.4.4.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> by ridge regression on <math id="S2.SS2.25.25.25.5.5.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{A}_{\mathrm{fit}},b_{\mathrm{fit}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{A}_{\mathrm{fit}},b_{\mathrm{fit}})</annotation></semantics></math> and restore the original library scale with <math id="S2.SS2.26.26.26.6.6.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}=D_{\mathrm{fit}}^{-1}\widetilde{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>fit</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}=D_{\mathrm{fit}}^{-1}\widetilde{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.29.29.29" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.29.29.29.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">6</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.29.29.29.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.29.29.29.3.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.29.29.29.3.3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">On each validation system, compute <math id="S2.SS2.27.27.27.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{s}(\mathcal{S})=\lVert A_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\hat{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}-b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\rVert_{2}^{2}/(\lVert b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\rVert_{2}^{2}+\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>val</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>val</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>val</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{s}(\mathcal{S})=\lVert A_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\hat{\xi}_{\mathcal{S}}-b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\rVert_{2}^{2}/(\lVert b_{\mathrm{val}}^{s}\rVert_{2}^{2}+\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. Record the mean <math id="S2.SS2.28.28.28.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> and standard error <math id="S2.SS2.29.29.29.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{se}(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>se</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{se}(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.32.32.32" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.32.32.32.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row">7</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.32.32.32.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify">
<span id="S2.SS2.32.32.32.3.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.32.32.32.3.3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Let <math id="S2.SS2.30.30.30.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\min}\in\arg\min_{\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}_{\tau}}\mu(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\min}\in\arg\min_{\mathcal{S}\in\mathcal{C}_{\tau}}\mu(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math> and admit every <math id="S2.SS2.31.31.31.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S2.SS2.32.32.32.3.3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\mathcal{S})\leq\mu(\mathcal{S}_{\min})+\mathrm{se}(\mathcal{S}_{\min})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>se</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\mathcal{S})\leq\mu(\mathcal{S}_{\min})+\mathrm{se}(\mathcal{S}_{\min})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
<tr id="S2.SS2.33.33.33" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.33.33.33.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom:2.0pt;">8</th>
<td id="S2.SS2.33.33.33.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_justify" style="padding-bottom:2.0pt;">
<span id="S2.SS2.33.33.33.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.33.33.33.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">Select the admissible support lexicographically by <math id="S2.SS2.33.33.33.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(\mathcal{S}),-v(\mathcal{S}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(|\mathcal{S}|,\mu(\mathcal{S}),-v(\mathcal{S}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
<tfoot class="ltx_tfoot">
<tr id="S2.SS2.35.35.35" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.SS2.35.35.35.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" colspan="2">
<span id="S2.SS2.35.35.35.2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS2.35.35.35.2.2.2" class="ltx_p" style="width:433.6pt;"><span id="S2.SS2.35.35.35.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> selected support <math id="S2.SS2.34.34.34.1.1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and coefficients <math id="S2.SS2.35.35.35.2.2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\xi}_{\widehat{\mathcal{S}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ξ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\xi}_{\widehat{\mathcal{S}}}</annotation></semantics></math> fitted on the independent fit system and mapped to the original library scale.</span>
</span>
</th>
</tr>
</tfoot>
</table>
<span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#S2.SS2" title="B.2 Selection Algorithm and Configuration ‣ B Stability-Validated Weak Selection ‣ Freeze, Then Select: Structured Field Adapters and Stability-Validated Weak Selection for PDE Discovery from Sparse Observations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> summarizes SVWS. It assigns support generation,
coefficient fitting, and validation to disjoint weak systems built from the
same frozen field. Independently shifted patch grids provide different weak
views: generation systems produce candidate supports across sparsity levels,
the fit system estimates their physical coefficients, and validation systems
compare the fitted equations on held-out patches. All three stages operate
after the adapter is frozen.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="S2.SS2.p2.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{g}=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{g}=12</annotation></semantics></math> generation systems and the threshold multipliers
<math id="S2.SS2.p2.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0.25,0.5,0.75,1,1.25,1.5,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.75</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0.25,0.5,0.75,1,1.25,1.5,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>
around the base STLSQ threshold. The resulting <math id="S2.SS2.p2.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12\times 7=84" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12\times 7=84</annotation></semantics></math> support
proposals are deduplicated, and term recurrence is computed over all
generation-system and threshold-multiplier pairs. Terms with recurrence at
least <math id="S2.SS2.p2.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> define the stable candidate pool.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Each retained support is refitted by ridge regression on one independent fit
system and evaluated on <math id="S2.SS2.p3.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{v}=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{v}=7</annotation></semantics></math> independently shifted validation systems. The
STLSQ solves and fixed-support refits both use ridge <math id="S2.SS2.p3.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, with at most
20 STLSQ iterations; the normalized validation risk uses
<math id="S2.SS2.p3.3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math>. Columns are normalized during STLSQ and coefficient
fitting, then mapped back to the physical library scale before validation. The
base thresholds for KdV, KS, and 2D AD are <math id="S2.SS2.p3.4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p3.5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4</annotation></semantics></math>,
respectively. These settings were selected using development seeds
<math id="S2.SS2.p3.7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{42,505,606,808,909\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>505</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>606</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>808</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>909</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{42,505,606,808,909\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then shared across S20 and T20 and fixed for all test
seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">C </span>External Baseline Implementations</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All baselines receive the sampled observations and physical candidate
libraries used in the main comparison. Each retains the optimization and
support selection procedure specified by its source implementation or
published algorithm. PDE-FIND and WSINDy operate on a shared spectral
reconstruction of the samples, whereas the neural methods use the observations
in their data objectives. Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table S4 ‣ C External Baseline Implementations ‣ Freeze, Then Select: Structured Field Adapters and Stability-Validated Weak Selection for PDE Discovery from Sparse Observations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S4</span></a> identifies
the implementation, observation interface, and coefficient readout for each
method. Settings not specified by the original source are chosen on
development seeds and fixed before evaluation.</p>
</div>
